research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:9:## Results and interpretation
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:11:[Comparison chart](results-v1/results.html), [compact metrics](results-v1/metrics.json), [complete raw summary](../../../runs/memory-retention-2026-11-01/long-term-memory-v1-live-pilot-v1/summary.json).
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:18:| Combined, absent feedback | 4/4 | 2/4 | 2/4 | Fail |
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:19:| Combined, matched-shuffled feedback | 3/4 | 3/4 | 3/4 | Fail |
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:22:Each count is a positive-margin ranking among four associations; ties count as incorrect. Every seed/item/candidate value remains in the raw summary and phase snapshots. The absent system changes neural state under intrinsic dynamics despite no teacher event; its initial four correct rankings must not be presented as informative-feedback acquisition evidence.
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:24:During the 24 live reversal choices, Fly+memory and memory-only each choose correctly 23 times; Fly-only chooses correctly 12 times, before eventually ending with all four associations ranked correctly. Acquisition choices are respectively 95/96, 93/96 and 95/96. These are descriptive trajectories on **one** development seed, not a statistically established speed/accuracy advantage. Fixed score scaling, exploration and different chosen-action feedback histories are part of the comparison; do not call it a pure neural learning-rate improvement.
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:26:The memory-backed systems' own raw neural scores still prefer the old candidate for reversed item 0 at the final test. Their external records return -1 for that old action and +1 for the new action, so arbitration makes the correct choice. This is a visible external override, **not consolidation of the revised association into neural weights**. Fly-only follows a different action/feedback trajectory and eventually revises its neural ranking correctly.
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:30:## Integration
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:32:[Policy module](../../../.codebase/src/neural-learning/memory-backed-policy-v1.mjs): known exact recall has precedence in Fly+memory; otherwise its score comes from a fixed clipped neural value. Memory-only readout returns known recall or zero. Fly-only readout uses the same scaled neural value. No fitted mixing weight or backpropagation is introduced. Record the raw neural value, recalled event, selected score and live action before feedback.
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:36:The informative three-system comparison is accompanied by combined-system absent, within-block matched-shuffled and disabled-learning controls. All have 120 trials and 553 graph forwards; controls are not a full factorial comparison. The 16-frame noisy pilot delay differs from the old 400-frame experiment. Do not import old retention gates or infer biological time.
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:38:## Execution and persistence
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:40:[Registered run](../../../python%20actions/long-term-memory-v1-live-pilot-v1-step.json), [live artifacts](../../../runs/memory-retention-2026-11-01/long-term-memory-v1-live-pilot-v1/manifest.json). The graph process is serial and guarded at 2048 MiB RSS, 256 MiB free memory, duty .5, heap 256 MiB and a 5400-second wall ceiling. Do not relaunch it while its owner is live or unknown.
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:46:## Checks and completed audit
research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md:50:[Separate auditor](../../../.codebase/scripts/neural-learning/audit-long-term-memory-v1-live.mjs), [audit registration](../../../python%20actions/long-term-memory-v1-live-audit-v1-step.json), [passed output](audit-v1.json). After the complete summary was published, it checked all six conditions, 720 trial receipts, 4280 local neural update frames, 144 item evaluations and every phase snapshot, completing in 35.25 seconds with 110.84 MiB peak sampled RSS. It reconstructs local neural memory from logged activity, external entries, scores, random choices, synthetic feedback bindings, matched shuffle, all snapshots and outcomes. Recorded full-graph responses are not independently regenerated. Both implementations are authored in this agent session, so separate arithmetic is not an independent reviewer or experimental replicate.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:3:**Status: APPROVED 2026-10-30, with the researcher's definition of reasoning (section 2). The read-only eye test (section 7) may run after the decoder check below. Training may not start until the memory rule (section 5) has separate approval. The numbers in section 7 may change only from the decoder check, before any graph data exists.** Old runs stay as "early development" history. Their results do not count as evidence for this plan. Background: [restart handoff](../../handoffs/restart-handoff-2026-10-30.md).
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:11:## 1. Research question
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:13:Can a model built on the real fly wiring (134,209 neurons, 2,700,513 edges) see a chess board through its modelled eyes, get feedback only on its own choices, and learn a chess fact that its input does not state? Can it then use that fact on new kinds of position?
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:17:## 2. Definition of reasoning
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:22:2. The Fly gets the fact from feedback on its own choices.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:37:## 3. Input
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:42:2. **Piece shape.** The earlier eye tests gave each square one brightness: mover, opponent or empty. That input had no piece type, so it could not contain the safe/unsafe answer. New rule: each piece type is a fixed small picture, drawn on the square. Each photoreceptor samples the picture at its stored position (`retina_uv`). Colour sets the brightness.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:52:## 4. Feedback rule
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:56:3. The independent checker verifies the chosen move only. A safe capture gives a reward pulse. An unsafe capture or a quiet move gives a punishment pulse. Unknown gives no pulse.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:57:4. The pulse goes through the modelled dopamine neurons while the chosen move's image is active. No code changes a weight directly.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:61:## 4A. neuron-reader: observation first, then a justified move score
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:63:**Focused repair plan, 2026-10-31:** [neuron-reader module design](../neural-learning/neuron-reader.md) maps every review finding to its specific fix and check. It gives the two-function interface, exact 14-cell roster, sampling/pooling rules, coefficient decisions and acceptance checks. Use that document for reader implementation; this section retains the experimental order and permissions.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:69:### Passive recording contract [choice]
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:77:### Scalar move-score contract: unresolved until reconciled with memory
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:81:1. **Resolve each coefficient from evidence.** Record the source, exact cell/driver population, assay/manipulation, observed effect and limits. Behavioral valence, transmitter/fast-edge polarity, dopamine teaching sign and plasticity direction are different things. Unknown behavioral signs remain recorded with coefficient 0. Require at least one justified nonzero coefficient; do not fit coefficients to checker labels, Stockfish scores or sealed positions. A behavioral interpretation from a fly assay does not establish innate chess value.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:82:2. **Match the memory mechanism.** Check which observed cells the separately approved memory rule can actually change, and which model states it can reach. Verify that informative feedback can both raise and lower the relevant candidate margin against absent, matched-shuffled and disabled-plasticity controls in the separately declared memory test. Two numerical score signs are not required for ranking. If the reader misses needed memory targets, write an explicit revised roster and source rationale before data; do not silently add cells or alter the other session's mechanism.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:86:### Build order and stopping points
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:90:3. **Prepare the read-only eye protocol.** Resolve the already documented F03/F04 decisions, including the declared scope and feasible gain range of the usable-strength intervention, before registering that test. Source/coefficient research may proceed alongside this work. Passive recording and diagnostic decoding do not require a finalized deployed chooser or prior memory-rule selection; those would create a circular dependency with section 5. No new score or replacement numerical gate is selected by this revision.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:92:5. **After an eye-test pass, finalize the score with the separately approved memory rule.** Freeze the scalar/selection contract above and perform the separately approved real-route memory test. Informative feedback and matched controls must establish acquisition, retention and reversal before the existing chess training/transfer phases. Preserve the researcher approval boundary for the memory rule and the locked final tests. The source/target investigation can proceed earlier; this step is final selection, not a demand to stop the other session's development assays.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:94:## 5. Memory rule
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:98:1. **Today's problem.** The alpha1/alpha3 rule is `dg = eta*D*k`, with `D` never positive. Gains only fall, to a floor of 0.2 ([code](../../../.codebase/src/neural-learning/alpha-lobe-memory.mjs)). The older gamma-side rule has a recovery term, `dg = eta*D*(k+g-1)`, so a gain can recover toward 1 but cannot pass it.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:100:   - Handler et al. 2019: two dopamine receptors direct "either synaptic depression or potentiation", depending on the order of odour and dopamine. Figure legends name gamma4/gamma5. I read the abstract and legends only.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:101:   - Berry et al. 2018: one dopamine neuron pair (gamma2alpha'1) lowers and then restores the MBON response.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:103:   - Aso and Rubin 2016: alpha1 is the store most resistant to change. Alpha3 needs many repeats. Unpaired dopamine reduces memory in other compartments.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:106:5. **Hard rule.** No two-way rule enters training until the source register has its source, compartment and trigger. Any positive `D` must come from a modelled, source-backed trigger, not from the teacher.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:110:1. **Do not add strengthening.** Value is approach side minus avoid side, so weakening the opposite side already raises value. Felsenberg et al. 2018 report two opposing memory traces existing together in extinction. Our feedback comes after the image, which is forward timing, so depression is also the expected direction.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:111:2. **Stop the floor with slow recovery.** Use the existing equation `dg = eta*D*(k+g-1)`, where inactive KCs recover toward 1 when dopamine fires. Old evidence: this erased a one-lesson trace in about 10 lessons. So each compartment gets its own recovery rate, fast in gamma and slow in alpha. Aso and Rubin support different rates per compartment, but give no numbers we can copy. The rates are a free choice and must be fixed on development data only.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:112:3. **Let real wires limit learning.** The graph has 480 direct MBON-to-dopamine edges. MBON14 to PPL106 (118 synapses) and MBON12 to PPL103 (102) are excitatory, so learning should lower the later dopamine and slow itself. MBON07 to PAM11 (83) is inhibitory, so learning should raise later dopamine; this may fit the consolidation loop in Ichinose et al. 2015. Today's pulse is at the top of its range (dopamine factors about -1), so these wires may have no room to act (hypothesis). Bennett et al. 2021 model this idea as prediction error. I read the abstract only, and their connections are partly proposed, not measured.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:114:5. **Test memory before chess.** Use simple non-chess patterns on the real graph. Measure how many associations it holds, interference, reversal and retention over many lessons, against the published behaviour in section 5.2. If this fails, we do not train on chess.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:116:## 6. Comparators
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:129:1. Informative: own-choice feedback.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:130:2. No feedback.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:131:3. Matched shuffled feedback.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:133:5. Shuffled wiring with feedback.
documentation/design/research-goals/restart-plan-2026-10-30.md:134:6. Eyes straight to KCs, no graph, same memory rule.
